          "ruleIndex": 20,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "The owner of the escrow, 0x1111111111111111111111111111111111111111, is not the multisig of the file, so one key can change every rule of the escrow. The ethereum.org page on smart contract security calls one owner key a single point of failure and suggests a multi-signature account. Fix: Make the owner, the fee setter and the treasury the multisig, and the upgrader the multisig or a timelock it controls; set them in roles."
